arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a university course catalog. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-9df572f75d064572a38997d9adc8decc/UniversityCourseCatalog` using `dotnet new blazor -int Server --no-https`.

## Requirements
- Browse departments and courses in a searchable, filterable list
- View course detail pages (description, schedule, credits, instructor bio)
- Students submit an enrollment request form (name, student ID, course selection) — standard HTML form, no wizards or real-time validation
- Homepage shows featured courses and department links
- No authentication — open to all students and visitors
- Hosted on university intranet with fast, reliable connectivity

## Architecture Decisions
- **Per-page Interactive Server**: Only the Courses browse page gets `@rendermode InteractiveServer` (for search/filter). Everything else stays static SSR.
- **Enrollment form**: Uses SSR form handling with `[SupplyParameterFromForm]`, `EditForm`, and `AntiforgeryToken`. Standard POST, no interactivity needed.
- **Data**: In-memory sample data via a singleton service.
- **No auth**.

## Component Plan

### Component Tree
```
MainLayout / NavMenu
├── Home (page "/")
│   ├── FeaturedCourses → CourseCard
│   └── DepartmentLinks
├── Courses (page "/courses") - InteractiveServer
│   ├── CourseFilters
│   └── CourseList → CourseCard
├── CourseDetail (page "/courses/{id}")
└── Enroll (page "/enroll") - SSR form
```

### Models (create in `/Models/` folder)
```csharp
// Models/Department.cs
public class Department
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = "";
    public string Code { get; set; } = ""; // e.g. "CS", "MATH"
    public string Description { get; set; } = "";
}

// Models/Instructor.cs
public class Instructor
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = "";
    public string Title { get; set; } = ""; // e.g. "Associate Professor"
    public string Bio { get; set; } = "";
    public string Email { get; set; } = "";
}

// Models/Course.cs
public class Course
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Code { get; set; } = ""; // e.g. "CS 101"
    public string Title { get; set; } = "";
    public string Description { get; set; } = "";
    public int Credits { get; set; }
    public string Schedule { get; set; } = ""; // e.g. "MWF 10:00-10:50 AM"
    public string Location { get; set; } = "";
    public int DepartmentId { get; set; }
    public string DepartmentName { get; set; } = "";
    public int InstructorId { get; set; }
    public string InstructorName { get; set; } = "";
    public bool IsFeatured { get; set; }
    public int MaxEnrollment { get; set; }
    public int CurrentEnrollment { get; set; }
}

// Models/EnrollmentRequest.cs
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

public class EnrollmentRequest
{
    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Name is required.")]
    [StringLength(100, ErrorMessage = "Name cannot exceed 100 characters.")]
    public string StudentName { get; set; } = "";

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Student ID is required.")]
    [RegularExpression(@"^[A-Z]{2}\d{6}$", ErrorMessage = "Student ID must be in format XX000000 (2 letters followed by 6 digits).")]
    public string StudentId { get; set; } = "";

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    [Range(1, int.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    public int CourseId { get; set; }
}
```

### Service (create in `/Services/` folder)
```csharp
// Services/ICatalogService.cs
public interface ICatalogService
{
    List<Department> GetDepartments();
    Department? GetDepartment(int id);
    List<Course> GetCourses();
    List<Course> GetFeaturedCourses();
    List<Course> GetCoursesByDepartment(int departmentId);
    List<Course> SearchCourses(string? searchTerm, int? departmentId, int? credits);
    Course? GetCourse(int id);
    Instructor? GetInstructor(int instructorId);
    bool SubmitEnrollment(EnrollmentRequest request);
}

// Services/CatalogService.cs — singleton in-memory implementation with rich sample data
// Include at least 3 departments (Computer Science, Mathematics, English) 
// with 3-4 courses each, and 4-5 instructors with realistic bios.
```

## Implementation Steps

1. **Delete template pages**: Remove `Components/Pages/Counter.razor`, `Components/Pages/Weather.razor`, `Components/Pages/Error.razor` (we'll recreate Error), and any related files.

2. **Create Models**: Create `/Models/` directory and all model files.

3. **Create Services**: Create `/Services/` directory, `ICatalogService.cs` and `CatalogService.cs` with rich sample data.

4. **Register service in Program.cs**: Add `builder.Services.AddSingleton<ICatalogService, CatalogService>();` and add the using for services/models.

5. **Update _Imports.razor**: Add `@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Models` and `@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Services`.

6. **Update MainLayout.razor**: University-themed layout with a navigation bar (Home, Courses, Enroll links). Keep it clean with a header/nav/main/footer structure. Use CSS isolation (`MainLayout.razor.css`).

7. **Create shared components in `Components/Shared/`**:
   - `CourseCard.razor` — displays a course summary card (code, title, credits, instructor, department). Has a `[Parameter] Course Course` and a link to detail page.

8. **Create page components in `Components/Pages/`**:
   - `Home.razor` — `@page "/"`. Shows a hero section, featured courses (uses `CourseCard`), and department links section. All static SSR.
   - `Courses.razor` — `@page "/courses"`. Has `@rendermode InteractiveServer`. Contains search box, department filter dropdown, credits filter. Displays filtered `CourseCard` list.
   - `CourseDetail.razor` — `@page "/courses/{Id:int}"`. Static SSR. Shows full course info: title, code, description, schedule, location, credits, instructor name/title/bio/email. Has a link to enroll.
   - `Enroll.razor` — `@page "/enroll"`. Static SSR form. Uses `EditForm` with `[SupplyParameterFromForm]`. Fields: student name, student ID, course selection dropdown. Shows success message after submission. Include `<AntiforgeryToken />` since it's SSR. Support an optional `?courseId=X` query parameter to pre-select the course.
   - `Error.razor` — `@page "/Error"`. Simple error page.
   - `NotFound.razor` — `@page "/not-found"`. Simple 404 page.

9. **Add CSS**: Create `wwwroot/app.css` or update existing CSS with a clean, professional university theme. Use a blue/navy color scheme. The CSS should handle:
   - Navigation bar styling
   - Course card grid layout
   - Form styling
   - Hero section on homepage
   - Responsive design basics
   - Detail page layout

10. **Create AGENTS.md** in the project root with this content (replace {AppName} with UniversityCourseCatalog):
```
# UniversityCourseCatalog

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| **Interactivity Mode** | Server |
| **Interactivity Scope** | Per-page |

## Rendering configuration
This project uses per-page Interactive Server with prerendering.
Created with `dotnet new blazor -int Server`.

Pages are static SSR by default. Only components that explicitly add `@rendermode InteractiveServer` become interactive.

## Adding new components
- Create new `.razor` files in `Components/Pages/` for routable pages or `Components/` for shared components.
- New pages are static SSR by default. Only add `@rendermode InteractiveServer` to components that need client-side behavior (live search, real-time updates, complex form interactions).
- Static pages can use standard HTML forms with `[SupplyParameterFromForm]` — no interactivity needed.

## Data access
- Components can inject services directly — no HTTP API layer needed.

## Don'ts
- Don't add `@rendermode InteractiveServer` to every page — keep read-only content static for performance and lower server memory.
- Don't inject `HttpContext` in interactive components — it's not available during SignalR circuit lifetime.
- Don't set `@rendermode` on `<Routes>` in `App.razor` — that makes it global. Per-page mode means individual components opt in.
```

## Important Implementation Notes

- For the Courses page with `@rendermode InteractiveServer`: Use `@bind` for the search input and filter dropdowns, with an `OnParametersSet` or button click to trigger filtering. Reactively filter as user types.
- For the Enroll page SSR form: Use `EditForm` with `Model` and `OnValidSubmit`. Use `[SupplyParameterFromForm]` to bind the model. Add `<DataAnnotationsValidator />` and `<ValidationSummary />`. After successful submission, show a success message. Use `[SupplyParameterFromQuery]` for the optional courseId parameter.
- CourseCard should link to `/courses/{Id}` for detail and have a subtle "Enroll" link to `/enroll?courseId={Id}`.
- The Courses page filtering should filter by search term (matches course title, code, or description), department, and credits.
- Make sure to use `formName` parameter on the `EditForm` and use `FormName` attribute on the form model, since this is SSR.

## Build and verify
After implementing everything, run `dotnet build` in the project directory to make sure it compiles without errors. Fix any issues.

