kind.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a university course catalog. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-9df572f75d064572a38997d9adc8decc/UniversityCourseCatalog` using `dotnet new blazor -int Server --no-https`.

## Requirements
- Browse departments and courses in a searchable, filterable list
- View course detail pages (description, schedule, credits, instructor bio)
- Students submit an enrollment request form (name, student ID, course selection) — standard HTML form, no wizards or real-time validation
- Homepage shows featured courses and department links
- No authentication — open to all students and visitors
- Hosted on university intranet with fast, reliable connectivity

## Architecture Decisions
- **Per-page Interactive Server**: Only the Courses browse page gets `@rendermode InteractiveServer` (for search/filter). Everything else stays static SSR.
- **Enrollment form**: Uses SSR form handling with `[SupplyParameterFromForm]`, `EditForm`, and `AntiforgeryToken`. Standard POST, no interactivity needed.
- **Data**: In-memory sample data via a singleton service.
- **No auth**.

## Component Plan

### Component Tree
```
MainLayout / NavMenu
├── Home (page "/")
│   ├── FeaturedCourses → CourseCard
│   └── DepartmentLinks
├── Courses (page "/courses") - InteractiveServer
│   ├── CourseFilters
│   └── CourseList → CourseCard
├── CourseDetail (page "/courses/{id}")
└── Enroll (page "/enroll") - SSR form
```

### Models (create in `/Models/` folder)
```csharp
// Models/Department.cs
public class Department
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = "";
    public string Code { get; set; } = ""; // e.g. "CS", "MATH"
    public string Description { get; set; } = "";
}

// Models/Instructor.cs
public class Instructor
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = "";
    public string Title { get; set; } = ""; // e.g. "Associate Professor"
    public string Bio { get; set; } = "";
    public string Email { get; set; } = "";
}

// Models/Course.cs
public class Course
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Code { get; set; } = ""; // e.g. "CS 101"
    public string Title { get; set; } = "";
    public string Description { get; set; } = "";
    public int Credits { get; set; }
    public string Schedule { get; set; } = ""; // e.g. "MWF 10:00-10:50 AM"
    public string Location { get; set; } = "";
    public int DepartmentId { get; set; }
    public string DepartmentName { get; set; } = "";
    public int InstructorId { get; set; }
    public string InstructorName { get; set; } = "";
    public bool IsFeatured { get; set; }
    public int MaxEnrollment { get; set; }
    public int CurrentEnrollment { get; set; }
}

// Models/EnrollmentRequest.cs
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

public class EnrollmentRequest
{
    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Name is required.")]
    [StringLength(100, ErrorMessage = "Name cannot exceed 100 characters.")]
    public string StudentName { get; set; } = "";

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Student ID is required.")]
    [RegularExpression(@"^[A-Z]{2}\d{6}$", ErrorMessage = "Student ID must be in format XX000000 (2 letters followed by 6 digits).")]
    public string StudentId { get; set; } = "";

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    [Range(1, int.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    public int CourseId { get; set; }
}
```

### Service (create in `/Services/` folder)
```csharp
// Services/ICatalogService.cs
public interface ICatalogService
{
    List<Department> GetDepartments();
    Department? GetDepartment(int id);
    List<Course> GetCourses();
    List<Course> GetFeaturedCourses();
