# UniversityCourseCatalog

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| **Interactivity Mode** | Server |
| **Interactivity Scope** | Per-page |

## Rendering configuration
This project uses per-page Interactive Server with prerendering.
Created with `dotnet new blazor -int Server`.

Pages are static SSR by default. Only components that explicitly add `@rendermode InteractiveServer` become interactive.

## Adding new components
- Create new `.razor` files in `Components/Pages/` for routable pages or `Components/` for shared components.
- New pages are static SSR by default. Only add `@rendermode InteractiveServer` to components that need client-side behavior (live search, real-time updates, complex form interactions).
- Static pages can use standard HTML forms with `[SupplyParameterFromForm]` — no interactivity needed.

## Data access
- Components can inject services directly — no HTTP API layer needed.

## Don'ts
- Don't add `@rendermode InteractiveServer` to every page — keep read-only content static for performance and lower server memory.
- Don't inject `HttpContext` in interactive components — it's not available during SignalR circuit lifetime.
- Don't set `@rendermode` on `<Routes>` in `App.razor` — that makes it global. Per-page mode means individual components opt in.
```

## Important Implementation Notes

- For the Courses page with `@rendermode InteractiveServer`: Use `@bind` for the search input and filter dropdowns, with an `OnParametersSet` or button click to trigger filtering. Reactively filter as user types.
- For the Enroll page SSR form: Use `EditForm` with `Model` and `OnValidSubmit`. Use `[SupplyParameterFromForm]` to bind the model. Add `<DataAnnotationsValidator />` and `<ValidationSummary />`. After successful submission, show a success message. Use `[SupplyParameterFromQuery]` for the optional courseId parameter.
- CourseCard should link to `/courses/{Id}` for detail and have a subtle "Enroll" link to `/enroll?courseId={Id}`.
- The Courses page filtering should filter by search term (matches course title, code, or description), department, and credits.
- Make sure to use `formName` parameter on the `EditForm` and use `FormName` attribute on the form model, since this is SSR.

## Build and verify
After implementing everything, run `dotnet build` in the project directory to make sure it compiles without errors. Fix any issues.

